module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.OmegaSixThree.OrthogonalityGraph.Coordinates
/-!
# Kernel-checked witnesses for local orthogonality geometry

Each pair of coordinate points has a common neighbor. For a distinct nonedge,
two adjacent common neighbors cover the common-neighbor set by their
neighborhoods. For an edge, six common neighbors have neighborhoods covering
all 117 vertices. These finite certificates imply exactly the local filling
properties in Aschbacher–Smith, Lemma F.5.8(2), printed pp. 303–304.

For each first vertex, `witnesses` packs 117 cells of 56 bits. Each cell has
eight seven-bit indices: the two centers followed by the six edge witnesses.
Unused entries are zero. `root_check`, `centers_check`, and `edge_check` check
all required memberships and covering identities by kernel reduction. Thus
neither the choice of these numbers nor an external search is trusted.
-/

@[expose] public section

